  "problem": "The third-order differential equation ${y}^{\u2034}-3{y}^{\u2032}+4y=0$\ncan be expressed as the matrix equation ${x}^{\u2032}(t)=Ax(t),$ where \n\n$$\nx(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & b & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ a & c & 0\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nand for $y=y(t),$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y={x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {y}^{\u2032}={x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {y}^{\u2033}={x}_{3}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the value of $a+b+c.$",
